    "body": "## Purpose \u2014 approved jems identity fidelity (active, not legacy UI)\nPR #33 established the universal jems experience; #35, #37 and #40 subsequently replaced and improved Studio, homepage, parent insights, profiles and Bubblegum. **This PR now carries only distinct brand fidelity work onto the current `main`**. It does **not** revert those UX/game releases.\n\n### Concrete value beyond main\n- Correct the exact six approved source-guide colors: **Ink #0B1E3B; Jem Blue #2E6BFF; Spark #8B5CF6; Play #FF5E7A; Idea #FFC24D; Build #22D3A6**. Keep Cloud #FFF7EE and Soft Lilac #E6D8FF. Preserve deeper semantic action shades where white-text contrast demands them.\n- Use the approved lowercase gem/wrench logo and THE GAME FACTORY subline as reproducible local SVG assets, including `jems-logo.svg`, `jems-mark.svg`, `arcade-icon.svg`, `jems-mono.svg`, `jems-reversed.svg`, `jems-pattern.svg`.\n- **Fix the original monochrome defect across BOTH old and new aliases:** the wrench center is solid opaque white, not a transparent hole. Keep existing URLs `jems-mark-monochrome.svg` and `jems-mark-inverse.svg`, corrected to the same geometry.\n- Update the PWA `jems-app-icon.svg` to embed the current gem and white wrench, with no external asset URLs; align standalone wordmark, facets, sparks, blocks, HTML meta theme and webmanifest with approved named swatches.\n- Keep text and voice distinct: accessible **Send to jems** for typed messages and **Speak** for supported microphone input. Preserve source and meanings of current game-build and session controls.\n- Add exact-color, asset-presence, white-wrench, PWA metadata, legacy-art consistency, desktop/phone and accessibility regression assertions. No fonts are downloaded or distributed without license.\n\n### Protected integrations\nRetain merged #37 parent learning insights, Math/English header, profile handling, dismissal/archive/restore/build cancellation; merged #40 sticker Bubblegum default + older physics versions; merged #35 conversation/build/experiment semantics; the `?arcade=1` escape route; Math/Language Arts required checkpoints, private data and safety defaults. New backgrounds are decoration only, never a substitute for the curated artwork/game controls.\n\n### Reconciliation and review\n- **Current exact PR head:** `feef265fe72ed55cddc8b2d89a0fbf2f1bb991e1`.\n- Base: `main`; previous old stack from #32/#33 no longer applies. The branch was integrated on top of `913ff559` (#40) without changing the newly merged UX.\n- Original source is the user-approved raster **Jems Brand Identity Style Guide**. The SVGs are manually reconstructed vector interpretations. CI verifies rendering and code contracts; **pixel-identical parity with the approved original is not automatically established**.\n- Full CI, exact-head [Arcade journeys](https://github.com/jzwyrzyk/family-game-factory/actions/runs/44358099463) and [jems full visual review](https://github.com/jzwyrzyk/family-game-factory/actions/runs/44358099367), plus final visual approval remain required before merge. Older branch CI is not valid.\n- Previous joy-contract failure was an obsolete assertion for the prior purple color. The test now asserts the approved Spark purple; new rerun verifies that correction.\n- Desktop/mobile screenshot artifacts must be reviewed for mark/wrench visibility, logo/wordmark legibility, header touch controls, responsive layout and contrast. Check installed app icon and black/white variants against the approved board as well.\n\n### Non-goals / release safety\nNo cloud infrastructure, API keys, paid AI, new child processing, P0 bypass, automatic public Pages publish or real-world release is authorized here. Brand asset parity does not claim that every interaction in the earlier 16-screen prototype is implemented. Keep **draft** until exact-head CI and owner art/visual sign-off, then squash-merge separately from deployment.\n",
    "title": "jems brand fidelity: exact approved palette, white-wrench lockups and universal UI",
