    "body": "## Intent\nMake the existing Jems brand feel rewarding across game creation without introducing a large cross-game economy or engine.\n\n**Gem Studio v1** extends merged #33's verified, nonblocking celebrations with a small, evidence-derived **rough \u2192 cut \u2192 polished** project gem and **Builder Levels 1\u20133**.\n\n### Implemented\n- Pure local logic maps saved child-authored ideas to rough gems; a saved experiment plus linked child reflection to cut; and a confirmed kept revision to polished.\n- Small on-brand gemstone artwork in *My jems* and next to Studio's existing truthful version label; compact builder level display only after a real idea exists.\n- A new verified cut/polish/level-up message uses the existing toast host. It cannot block taps, steal focus or create network requests.\n- No new localStorage key, new child information, new analytics, spend, daily streak, school-proficiency claim, remote change or game-code mutation.\n- Unit tests for absent/unverified activity, unknown experiment, runtime-only observation, confirmed improvement and levels.\n- Documents three starter games: **Mind Your Jems!** (#56), **Gem Factory** (separate follow-on), and **GemBots** (separate follow-on). No shared inventory, progress, cross-game dependency or giant platform refactor.\n\n### Existing overlap handled\n- #33 already celebrates confirmed creation milestones; this enhances it, not duplicates it.\n- #34 owns exact logo/palette fidelity. This PR uses existing assets and conservative matching colors; final visual reconciliation follows brand owner approval.\n- #54 learning evidence remains research-only; these builder labels do **not** claim math/language/computational mastery.\n- #55 adult/guardian safety permissions and #56 arcade mining are not modified.\n\n### Acceptance before merge\n- Exact-head **npm run build**, **npm run test:gem-progress**, full **npm test** and Studio/desktop/tablet/mobile browser workflows pass.\n- Validate local and remote kept versions, switching profiles, clear/archive, reloading with no repeat celebration, and reduced-motion interaction.\n- Visually approve polished-gem art, contrast, small-screen layout and nonintrusive popups.\n- Reconcile with later merged branding and platform work, and repeat CI on the final merge head.\n\n**Status: draft for implementation review. Not merged, deployed or verified passing.**",
    "title": "Jems Gem Studio \u2014 earned polished gems, builder levels & achievement delight",
